Subject: [PATCH] drm/bridge: waveshare-dsi: check the registered backlight

ws_bridge_probe() stores the result of ws_bridge_create_backlight() in
ws->backlight but then tests and decodes an uninitialized local
variable, so a failed backlight registration is never detected and the
probe path reads indeterminate stack contents. Test the stored pointer
and drop the unused local.

Found by source inspection for the house-panel FRDM retarget
(FRDM-GATE-BACKLIGHT); not yet exercised on hardware.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/waveshare-dsi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/waveshare-dsi.c
index efb3a2f..f54a22b 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/waveshare-dsi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/waveshare-dsi.c
@@ -150,7 +150,6 @@ static int ws_bridge_probe(struct i2c_client *i2c)
 	struct ws_bridge *ws;
 	struct drm_panel *panel;
 	int ret;
-	struct backlight_device *backlight;

 	ws = devm_kzalloc(dev, sizeof(*ws), GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!ws)
@@ -171,8 +170,8 @@ static int ws_bridge_probe(struct i2c_client *i2c)
 		return PTR_ERR(ws->next_bridge);

 	ws->backlight = ws_bridge_create_backlight(ws);
-	if (IS_ERR(backlight)) {
-		ret = PTR_ERR(backlight);
+	if (IS_ERR(ws->backlight)) {
+		ret = PTR_ERR(ws->backlight);
 		dev_err(dev, "Failed to create backlight: %d\n", ret);
 		return ret;
 	}
